From cfad81a2c1b58426c7859c6c59579ae5050dfa34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:59:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! Fog: Wind Waker HD's curve, the square of the
 GameCube's linear fog, while the host has HD's distances in place

HD's fog start before the camera on the draws' own fog too: a draw with linear
perspective fog from the game's clamped start (C 0) to the end of the host's
pair (its end is the projection's near x B / A) takes GXSetFog's A and C for
HD's start to that end. HD fogs its characters, plants and objects in their
own shaders with the same squared curve from that start; they kept the
clamped start. The lit scenery's draws take the same constants and the sun
pass's after-shade fog reads them, so it fogs from HD's start as before.
Ganon's Tower's far wall half: linear luminance 0.100 -> 0.111 (HD 0.123).
